-- title:
--   Jacobian criterion step: dv=0 forces v ∈ J I
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian ring, let $n \in \mathbb{N}$, and write $P = R[x_0,\dots,x_{n-1}]$ for the polynomial ring `MvPolynomial (Fin n) R`. Let $I \subseteq J$ be ideals of $P$ with $J$ maximal, and for each $N \in \mathbb{N}$ put $C_N = P/(J^N + J\,I)$ (the join $J^N \sqcup J*I$ of ideals being their sum). Suppose given a family of commutative rings $D_N$, each an $R$-algebra and a $C_N$-algebra compatibly (scalar tower $R \to C_N \to D_N$), such that $D_N$ is faithfully flat as a $C_N$-module, together with $R$-algebra homomorphisms $\sigma_N : P/I \to D_N$ subject to the following congruence: for every $N$ and every $f \in P$, the difference between $\sigma_N(f \bmod I)$ and the image in $D_N$ of $f \bmod (J^N + J\,I)$ lies in the ideal of $D_N$ generated by the image under $C_N \to D_N$ of the ideal $(J^N + I)/(J^N + J\,I)$ of $C_N$. The conclusion: any $v \in I$ all of whose partial derivatives $\partial v/\partial x_i$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\ n$) lie in $J$ lies in $J\,I$.
--
--   This is the Jacobian step underlying the criterion for formal smoothness at a closed point: it says that the map $I/J I \to \kappa \otimes_P \Omega_{P/R}$, $v \mapsto dv$, is injective once lifts of $P/I$ exist over faithfully flat covers of the small thickenings $P/(J^N + J I)$ of the truncations $P/(J^N + I)$. It is used by the two smoothness criteria [`AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_charP_of_finiteType_int`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_charP_of_finiteType_int) and [`AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_isNoetherianRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Smooth.of_forall_exists_lift_of_isArtinianRing_of_isNoetherianRing), which deduce smoothness from liftability along Artinian test rings.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvPolynomial_mem_mul_of_forall_pderiv_mem_of_forall_exists_algHom_lift.lean

